 `defineTheme` takes **design tokens only** (`colors` / `spacing` / `fontSize` / `radius` / `shadow`). Component "presets" (card/button style bundles) are user-land `.apply()` helpers, not `defineTheme`. The themeable unions are **closed** — a typo is a compile error, not an unstyled element at runtime.
 
 > **Why the `declare module` block?** A runtime call can't add to a compile-time type, so the typed-token magic needs one module augmentation. It's written **once** and *derives* its keys from `tokens` via `ThemeKeys<typeof tokens, "…">` — add tokens freely, never touch it again. Skip the block and tokens still work at runtime (CSS/safelist), you just lose autocomplete + typo-checking.
+
+### Class merge: `setClassMerge(theme)` (8.2.0, opt-in)
+
+Fluent methods append classes, so an override after a preset emits both and stylesheet order picks the winner. `setClassMerge(theme)`, called once at boot, turns on a serialize-time merge: within one element's `class`, a later class of the same family replaces the earlier one.
+
+```ts
+import { setClassMerge, type Tag } from "fluent-html";   // also on "fluent-html/render"
+import { theme } from "./theme";
+
+setClassMerge(theme);                       // process-wide, like setDevChecks
+const card = (t: Tag) => t.p("6").rounded("lg");
+Div().apply(card).p("4")                    // class="rounded-lg p-4" (card's p-6 dropped)
+Div().px("8").p("6")                        // both stay: px and p are different prefixes
+setClassMerge(false);                       // off again (the default)
+```
+
+- A family is the class's selector shape plus its exact CSS property set (Tailwind 4.3.3), per variant chain: `p-6 p-4` merges; `border-b border-line` and `text-lg text-primary` stay.
+- A strict-subset class (`text-[13px]`, a custom font-size token) is replaced by a later full class but never replaces one.
+- Never merged: `hidden`, cross-prefix pairs, important classes and unknown words (`cssClass("h-captcha").h("12")` keeps both).
+- The theme is the registry (`text-danger` is a color, `text-display` a size), so `setClassMerge(true)` is a type error.
+- Only emitted bytes change: `getClass()` returns every write. A class a client behavior flips (`toggleClass`, clipboard `feedback.class`) loses its earlier same-family class as a fallback.
 
