+#### Reading a built control's id: `getId()`
+
+A wrapper handed a built control (a field shell such as the template's `FormGroup`) reads its id with `getId()`: the id `Form<T>` stamped, `idPrefix` included, or `undefined` when none is set. `setFor()` drops the attribute on `undefined`, so branch on it:
+
+```typescript
+const Field = (text: string, input: Tag) =>
+  IfThenElse(input.getId(),
+    (id) => Div(Label(text).setFor(id), input),   // <label for="signup-email"> beside the control
+    () => Label(text, input));                    // no id: nest the control in its label
+```
+
+In a view that holds `f`, label a bound control with `f.label(name)` instead.
 
