+### IfNotEmpty / IfNotEmptyElse
+
+The list-shaped `IfThen`: `null`, `undefined` and `[]` all skip the branch, and the branch gets the list itself.
+
+```typescript
+import { IfNotEmpty, IfNotEmptyElse, ForEach } from 'fluent-html';
+
+IfNotEmpty(props.tags, (tags) => Ul(ForEach(tags, (t) => Li(t))))
+IfNotEmptyElse(orders, (os) => OrderTable(os), () => P("No orders yet"))
+```
+
+`IfThen(xs, …)` runs its branch for `[]` (an empty array is not null), so the container renders with no items, and a restated `xs.length > 0` guard loses the binding. A non-array argument names the fix: a boolean, string, number or `Set` goes to `IfThen`.
+
 ### Match
 
 `Match` maps a value to a view using an object of cases. TypeScript enforces exhaustiveness — if you miss a case, you get a compile error.
